<title>PAKISTAN: KARACHI ELECTRIC RISES 7.08 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>KARACHI ELECTRIC RISES 7.08 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-run Karachi Electric Supply Corporation's 10-rupee stock rose 2.00 rupees, or 7.08 percent, to 30.25 on Monday on the hope of its early privatisation, dealers at the Karachi Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>Heavy buying by some foreign fund managers pushed its price up in early trading, a dealer of Taurus Securities said.</p>
<p>&quot;The situation is not clear, but some fund managers expect its privatisation this year (1997/98 July-June)&quot;, he said.</p>
<p>About 1.3 million shares had changed hands in early trade, he added.</p>
